  "oneLiner": "The HSK 3.0 (2026) words that rank in the 500 most frequent Chinese words overall. This is fewer than 500 cards, by design — see the description.",
  "description": "Frequency rank here is global: it is measured across 118,765 upstream headwords, most of which are proper nouns, variants and function words that the HSK syllabus does not list. This pack is the intersection — every HSK 3.0 (2026) headword whose global rank is 500 or better — so it deliberately contains materially fewer than 500 words. The `size` field is the real card count; the 500 in the name is the frequency cutoff, not a quantity. Words whose frequency rank is unknown cannot appear in any Core pack at all; the canon's coverage figures record how many that is.",
  "rationale": "'Core 500' is a query people type, so the pack keeps the name. What it must not do is let the name imply a card count it does not deliver — a learner who expects 500 cards and receives fewer has been misled by the title, which is why the arithmetic is stated three times before anyone opens the file.",
